confirmation_body.description:
Plain-text body of the confirmation mail. The {confirmation_link}
placeholder is replaced by the link, which is appended when the
placeholder is missing; empty means a built-in text.

redirect_url.description:
Page the visitor is sent to when submit_action is redirect: required
then, and must start with http:// or https://. At most 512 characters;
stored unchecked for message forms.

company_record.description:
The linked company, loaded only by GET /leads/{id} (its
customer_count, lead_count and deal_count are 0 there, not computed);
omitted elsewhere.

honeypot_field.description:
Name of the decoy input the renderer must include and hide from people;
always "website_url_confirm". A non-empty value in the submission files
it as spam.

